{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1476178-spirit-bestiary","id":1476178,"title":"Spirit Bestiary","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-03-10T17:11:14-08:00","id":1476178,"title":"Spirit Bestiary","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> I am mainly interested in Mage, and I keep seeing posts similar to &quot;<i>Spirit is the best sphere because it can do everything</i>&quot;, I think the idea is that if you can find a spirit that has a charm that does what you need there is no need for other spheres.<br /> <br /> My question is, where are the spirit lists? I am only aware of spirits with stats on: KotE Core, W20 Core, W20 Umbral Velvet Shadow, M20 Gods &amp; Monsters.<br /> <br /> Is there a compiled list of all spirits somewhere? And if there is not, can you guys help me with other book names?<br /> <br /> Thanks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 03-11-2022, 08:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-11T09:33:41-08:00","id":1476213,"title":"","content":"They were always spread out all over the place, frankly. There's always Bygone Bestiary for ideas, though it'll need some tinkering with the rules. I use BB for chimera in C20 and it works well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-11T10:40:10-08:00","id":1476216,"title":"","content":"It's nice to see others thinking about this concept as well. Spirit sphere can do almost everything, except for time and a few powers of Prime or Correspondence effects (which paradox spirits and very strong creatures beyond reality can help with)... The only problem (if you don't use the golden rule) is that by the rules you need a sphere that &quot;resonates&quot; with the spirit to summon (elementals are an example of this). I'm afraid there is no list of all spirits and no book describing all the abilities of spirits. They are often used as an instrument for the ST or the player.<br /> <br /> In addition to those books, the following may help: <b>Book of the Wyld</b>; <b>Book of the Weaver</b>; <b>Possessed</b> (book) - some information about... possessed?; <b>Book of Wyrm + </b><b>WTA: Freak Legion: A Players Guide to Fomori</b>(mostly fomori, but there are stats for spirits); <b>Wraith: The Oblivion</b> or <b>Changelings </b>(Sounds like a joke, but they can be strong); <b>Infernalism: The Path of Screams </b>(for few demons and potential deities/totems); <b>M20: Falle</b>n (More for infernalism and some variety / greater understanding of the &quot;dark&quot; worlds and their inhabitants) &amp; <b>Bygone</b> (some can be spirits, some can be mythical beasts... or both). Also, some breed-books or tradition books can have little information. + My favorite: <b>Devil's Due </b>(There are stats for your own angel or you can use powers and pacts to create a normal spirit of nature, let ST and you decide what to do with it).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25408,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari","user":"Alphari","date":". 03-11-2022, 01:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari","name":"Alphari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25408_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-11T12:32:23-08:00","id":1476222,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the answers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alphari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1476178-spirit-bestiary?p=1476216#post1476216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only problem (if you don't use the golden rule) is that by the rules you need a sphere that &quot;resonates&quot; with the spirit to summon (elementals are an example of this).</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you explain this? You need another sphere besides Spirit to summon spirits? Even better, can you provide a page or reference for this? I use M20.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-11T14:18:32-08:00","id":1476226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1476178-spirit-bestiary?p=1476222#post1476222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you explain this? You need another sphere besides Spirit to summon spirits? Even better, can you provide a page or reference for this? I use M20.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was a little mistaken, maybe in the old books it was required (I looked for interesting rotes in them, but found a lot of strange solutions in terms of paradigm and logic... so I need to check). But what has remained unchanged is magic through spiritual-possession. There is an example in <b>M20</b> of a shaman who summons a wolf spirit for possession and uses this state for his own purposes. He needs spheres of spirit and life to manipulate himself (grow some teeth or claws, wolf-fur).<br /> <br /> <b>Yes, you can safely summon elementals to do their work for you by using only spirit 4</b>. + There is a possibility to get their powers. Possession in which the spirit can share their charms, there are a couple of examples in the old books (especially with demons and banes) + in the book &quot;<b>gods and monsters</b>&quot; there is an owl spirit (gives free spiritual powers based on your fears + seems to increase the maximum capacity of the quintessence). This is more a question for books of werewolves, demons/infernalists and spirits. They describe well these possessed and gifts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25408,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari","user":"Alphari","date":". 03-12-2022, 05:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari","name":"Alphari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25408_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-12T06:45:32-08:00","id":1476270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1476178-spirit-bestiary?p=1476213#post1476213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They were always spread out all over the place, frankly. There's always Bygone Bestiary for ideas, though it'll need some tinkering with the rules. I use BB for chimera in C20 and it works well.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Gods and Monsters supplement is pretty much an update to Bygone Bestiary","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-12T10:41:13-08:00","id":1476275,"title":"","content":"Axis Mundi: Book of Spirits","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-12T15:50:36-08:00","id":1476291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.pen-paper.net/indices/wod/spirits.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.pen-paper.net/wp-content/themes/magazine-basic/library/images/404.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.pen-paper.net/indices/wod/spirits.pdf\" target=\"_blank\"> Page not found &ndash; Pen &amp; Paper News </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.pen-paper.net/indices/wod/spirits.pdf\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.pen-paper.net/indices/wod/spirits.pdf </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-12T20:58:52-08:00","id":1476312,"title":"","content":"One aspect you need to remember for spirits is that they're thinking, feeling entities with their own wills, desires, and relationships.<br /> <br /> If a mage doesn't respect proper chiminage and just forcibly compels a spirit willy nilly, they' might just end up with a host of angry magical creatures that called that spirit a friend.<br /> <br /> The spirit sphere is powerful yeah, but it's also the sphere that Requires diplomacy and careful exchanges of favors. If you don't, the paradox spirits won't even Need to intervene other than to help clean the magical grease-stain that used to be a mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6383,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","user":"Prometheas","date":". 03-13-2022, 02:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-13T05:49:49-07:00","id":1476321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1476178-spirit-bestiary?p=1476270#post1476270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The Gods and Monsters supplement is pretty much an update to Bygone Bestiary</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, pretty shit update to be honest. Especially when you explicitly need Bygone Bestiary if you want to work with classical Bygones like Dragons, Rocs, Unicorns, etc.<br /> A must-have for Dragon player characters in fact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27335-technoma","name":"Technoma","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-16T03:57:06-07:00","id":1476514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1476178-spirit-bestiary?p=1476312#post1476312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One aspect you need to remember for spirits is that they're thinking, feeling entities with their own wills, desires, and relationships.<br /> <br /> If a mage doesn't respect proper chiminage and just forcibly compels a spirit willy nilly, they' might just end up with a host of angry magical creatures that called that spirit a friend.<br /> <br /> The spirit sphere is powerful yeah, but it's also the sphere that Requires diplomacy and careful exchanges of favors. If you don't, the paradox spirits won't even Need to intervene other than to help clean the magical grease-stain that used to be a mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is all true, too, and I nearly made a similar comment. It's easy enough to dial the spirits' hotline with the Spirit Sphere, and you might even be able to compel them to listen and act, but there are always consequences for that. A spirit pushed to do things they don't want to, or even just being pushed, might want revenge. Sooner or later, you're bound to muck things up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}